# Changelog Maintenance

`CHANGELOG.md` follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com) format with [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org).

## Entry anatomy

Every entry must capture three things:

| Field | Question it answers |
|---|---|
| **Intent** | What was the goal of this change? |
| **Rationale** | Why was this approach chosen? |
| **Impact** | How did it affect the codebase and user experience? |

## Format

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed
- **Intent:** <what you set out to do>
  **Rationale:** <why this way>
  **Impact:** <what changed for users and the codebase>
```

## When to update

- After every meaningful feature addition, change, fix, or removal.
- Before releasing a version: move items from `[Unreleased]` to a versioned block.
- Do NOT record trivial chores (whitespace, typo in a comment) unless they affect behaviour.

## Do / Don't

```
✅ DO: "Added streaming support. Rationale: reduces time-to-first-token for large outputs. Impact: new --stream flag; existing callers unaffected."
❌ DON'T: "Updated stuff."
❌ DON'T: Detailed function-level implementation notes (those belong in commit messages).
```
